<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">French Madagascar</h1><p class="st-meta">1897 CE – 1958 CE · capital Antananarivo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Madagascar as a French colony, from the overthrow of the Merina monarchy to the autonomous Malagasy Republic of 1958.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the conquest of 1895 and the end of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-madagascar">French Protectorate of Madagascar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed the island in 1896. In February 1897 the governor-general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-gallieni">Joseph Gallieni</a> abolished the Merina monarchy and exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-iii">Queen Ranavalona III</a> to Réunion and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, then put down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menalamba-rebellion">Menalamba rising</a> and subdued the coastal peoples.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gallieni and his successors imposed a head tax and forced labour, promoted French over English schooling and broke the power of the Merina elite. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">Coffee</a>, vanilla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> were exported, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nosy-be">Nosy Be</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/diego-suarez-colony">Diego-Suarez</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> were attached. In 1942 British forces took the island from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vichy-france">Vichy France</a>, and it passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-france">Free French</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The nationalist uprising of 1947 was crushed with tens of thousands of deaths. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> became the autonomous Malagasy Republic in October 1958 and fully independent on 26 June 1960 under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philibert-tsiranana">Philibert Tsiranana</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-madagascar.jpg" alt="French Madagascar" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1897 CE – 1958 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Antananarivo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Joseph Gallieni, Philibert Tsiranana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, Malagasy traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Colony of Madagascar and Dependencies</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=french-madagascar" aria-label="French Madagascar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5966 2878 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Madagascar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6286 3134L6286 3134M6286 3134L6193 3185M6286 3134L6286 3134M6286 3134L5054 728M6286 3134L6324 2930M6286 3134L6357 3061M6286 3134L6243 2910"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0M6193 3185h0M6286 3134h0M5054 728h0M6324 2930h0M6357 3061h0M6243 2910h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6286 3134h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Antananarivo. <a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=french-madagascar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
